      "sha256": "8af3b7c558ccf8421fdc0cb6a724a8cc82db802b65f56ae236a38b0621e85896",
      "bytes": 135615,
      "pages": 1,
      "title_tex": "Even and odd alignments of one ordered four-ligand frame.",
      "legend_tex": "Colored numbered balls identify ligand references, the gray digit beside each position identifies the frame slot, and the strip below each center repeats the same state as the ordered tuple read in slot order. All four centers share one fixed geometric frame. It contains two in-plane bonds, a bold wedge at slot 3 toward the viewer, and a hashed bond at slot 4 away from it. Only the assignment of ligands to slots changes. (A) The even 3-cycle \\(\\epsilon=(1\\;2\\;3)\\in A_4=\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{tet}}\\) sends \\(u=(1,2,3,4)\\) to \\((2,3,1,4)\\). Green marks a configuration-preserving action, a rigid rotation of the same local state. (B) The odd transposition \\(\\rho=(1\\;2)\\notin A_4\\) sends \\(u\\) to \\((2,1,3,4)\\). Blue marks the opposite orbit and uses the same verdict colors as Figure~\\ref{fig:orbit-examples}. The ledger states the coset decomposition \\(S_4=A_4\\sqcup\\rho A_4\\) behind Proposition~\\ref{prop:local-parity}: four distinct references admit 24 ordered frames that split \\(12+12\\) into two mirror-image configuration orbits.",
      "title_words": 9,
      "conservative_legend_words": 180,
      "all_fonts_embedded": true,
      "caption_removed_from_graphic": true,
      "crop_margin_points": 1,
      "rendered_acs_percentage_checked": null,
