    {
      "figure_number": 2,
      "label": "fig:support-motivation",
      "file": "Figure_02.pdf",
      "sha256": "e4568217e9190b1b84262d29d9dc46adbece17114171dd66a12d60930fe2441d",
      "bytes": 144781,
      "pages": 1,
      "title_tex": "Typed supports for configured stereochemical elements.",
      "legend_tex": "The support of a stereo element is a subgraph of prescribed shape, and the six families differ in that shape rather than in their algebra. Each header states the support type together with the arity and geometry group where the family uses a finite frame. Vermilion marks the carrier, blue marks the orientation datum, and green distinguishes the second terminal plane in panel C. (A) An atom support is one vertex; the two tetrahedral states share a single constitution and are exchanged by the mirror \\(\\sigma\\). (B) A bond support is one edge carrying two terminal pairs. (C) An axis support is a cumulated path whose termini lie in orthogonal planes, shown here in projection along the axis. (D) A path support is an ordered vertex sequence taken modulo canonical reversal; helicity is the sense of the rise \\(h\\). (E) A plane support is an oriented face whose off-plane pilot \\(p\\) fixes the sense of the normal \\(\\hat n\\). (F) A global support couples frames over a whole component; its joint configuration is retained explicitly. The footer ramp orders the six carriers by spatial extent and defines no inheritance between them. Molecular chirality, including a \\emph{meso} verdict, is a downstream whole-stereograph classification rather than a seventh carrier family.",
      "title_words": 6,
      "conservative_legend_words": 209,
      "all_fonts_embedded": true,
      "caption_removed_from_graphic": true,
      "crop_margin_points": 1,
      "rendered_acs_percentage_checked": null,
      "page_size": "481 x 310 pts",
      "preview": "previews/Figure_02.png"
    },
    {
      "figure_number": 3,
      "label": "fig:pipeline",
      "file": "Figure_03.pdf",
      "sha256": "29222db909a816e59a47a88dd10201df8c9aae88de90bdbfbcf16e57a4a38842",
      "bytes": 114525,
      "pages": 1,
      "title_tex": "One-way, fail-closed information flow, written as typed objects and the maps between them.",
      "legend_tex": "Stage~1 is configuration-neutral perception and returns potential carriers with configuration \\(\\bot\\). Only authorized evidence \\(\\operatorname{Auth}\\) may apply the attachment map \\(\\operatorname{att}\\) of Definition~\\ref{def:attachment}, which produces the configured stereograph \\(\\mathcal X\\). The declared support boundary \\(B\\) is audited before the expansion \\(\\Phi_\\chi\\) and the exact certificate \\(C^\\chi_{\\mathrm{SG}}\\); a failed audit refuses instead of returning a partial identity. The mirror map \\(\\mu\\) compares the certificate of \\(\\mathcal X\\) with that of its mirror image \\(\\overline{\\mathcal X}\\) and returns one or two classes. Derived CIP naming is an optional consumer. The footer states the two structural invariants: absent, configured, and molecularly chiral are three distinct predicates, and no downstream stage feeds information back into stages 1--3.",
      "title_words": 13,
      "conservative_legend_words": 125,
      "all_fonts_embedded": true,
      "caption_removed_from_graphic": true,
      "crop_margin_points": 1,
