      "pages": 1,
      "title_tex": "The two remaining declared task-boundary differences in the 258-record source-declared-configuration audit.",
      "legend_tex": "Orange circles mark atoms carrying explicit source \\code{@}/\\code{@@} configurations; wedge/hash bonds show the corresponding local orientation. In A, chemical identity preserves the genuine \\(\\mathrm{S{-}I}/\\mathrm{S{\\equiv}I}\\) distinction and returns chiral, whereas the ACS connectivity-only profile returns achiral. In D, the exact mirror isomorphism fixes the central configured carbon and exchanges the two configured cages, so the represented local configurations compensate in a meso-like, mirror-fixed arrangement. This is not a general meso assignment: the historical source-declared protocol lacks the coupled relation. The separate global certificate encodes the topology-completion probes as one orientation-unspecified framework and proves the ACS chiral outcome without reinterpreting the three source tags.",
